  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian Shelter Assistance for Vulnerable Populations Affected by Conflict in Ituri and North Kivu, Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM is implementing a shelter/non-food items sector project for populations affected by the conflict involving the M23 and the Allied Democratic Forces, which has led to an exacerbation of vulnerabilities, deterioration of living conditions, and an increase in humanitarian needs and population displacement in the Democratic Republic of the Congo. This project is part of IOM&apos;s programmatic strategy to ensure continuity of current humanitarian emergency response activities in North Kivu and Ituri provinces in particular, as well as an extension into areas of intervention where the severity of needs requires rapid emergency interventions. Under this project, IOM is committed to ensuring an effective response and is contributing to the achievement of the priority: emergency assistance for shelter upgrades for internally displaced persons in the host community. Through this intervention, IOM is proposing an upgrade of these shelters that provide displaced households and host community members with larger housing and sanitary facilities (family latrines) according to Sphere standards, offering more dignity and safety to the affected population.</narrative>
  </description>
